hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15962","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu Isra'il, he said, I heard Ja'da, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw a fat man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began gesturing to his belly with his hand, saying: Had this been elsewhere, it would have been better for you."
"15963","He said: And a man was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: This one intended to kill you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have no fear, you have no fear; had you intended that, Allah would not have given you power over me."
"15964","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us in the house of Qatada, he said, I heard Ja'da, who is the freed slave of Abu Isra'il, say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man was recounting a dream to him, and he mentioned his fatness and greatness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had this been elsewhere, it would have been better for you."
